In addition, an over-emphasis on creativity can lead to a lack of rigor in the design thinking process. When creativity is the primary focus, there may be less emphasis on evaluating the feasibility and scalability of solutions, as well as less attention paid to the financial and operational aspects of implementing solutions. This can result in solutions that are not practical or sustainable in the long-term.

