{"model": "Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B", "prompt": "Construction projects involve risks, and latent conditions are one of the most significant risks faced by contractors and principals. Latent conditions are physical conditions on or near a site that could not have been reasonably anticipated by a contractor at the time of tendering. These conditions can cause significant additional costs and delays in a construction project, which is why it is essential to understand what latent conditions mean and how to manage them.

In this article, we will explore the concept of latent conditions in construction projects, what constitutes a latent condition, and how to manage the risks associated with them. We will also discuss the importance of determining who bears the risk of latent conditions before entering into a contract or site investigation and the factors that should be considered when deciding how to manage the risks of latent conditions.

By understanding latent conditions and how to manage them, contractors and principals can minimize their risks and avoid costly disputes that may arise from unexpected physical conditions on a construction site.", "max_tokens": 27, "ignore_eos": true, "stream": true, "stream_options": {"include_usage": true}}

